From 96d055ad821122f2aec4290b2f3d6df2b27c0c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Yu <josephyu@yahooinc.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:26:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Do not put the PNG context in 32-bit-only memory

Opening the map screen rebooted the device. Decoded:

    0x4208e677 initPNGDecoder
    0x4207bd45 TFTView_320x240::loadMap
    0x42078071 TFTView_320x240::ui_event_MapButton
    0x4204002e lv_event_send

StoreProhibited inside initPNGDecoder, at the placement-new that constructs
PNG() in the buffer it just allocated:

    pngBuffer = heap_caps_malloc(sizeof(PNG), MALLOC_CAP_INTERNAL | MALLOC_CAP_32BIT);
    ...
    png = ::new (pngBuffer) PNG();

MALLOC_CAP_32BIT does not mean "aligned to 32-bit words", which is what the
comment above it says it was for. It means "only 32-bit accesses are legal in
this region", and on ESP32-S3 it can return IRAM. The PNG constructor does
byte-sized stores, and a byte store to such a region faults.

MALLOC_CAP_8BIT asks for the byte-addressable internal SRAM that was actually
wanted; allocations from it are word-aligned anyway.

Upstream code, from bcb327f (CURLService, #353) - not something this branch
introduced. Worth reporting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VjqMrWWLWXvmh69rvGCEo
---
 source/util/PNGdecoder.cpp | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/util/PNGdecoder.cpp b/source/util/PNGdecoder.cpp
index 0fc438e..608c25b 100644
--- a/source/util/PNGdecoder.cpp
+++ b/source/util/PNGdecoder.cpp
@@ -17,8 +17,14 @@ void initPNGDecoder(void)
 {
     static void *pngBuffer = nullptr;
     if (!pngBuffer) {
-        // force allocation into zero-wait-state Internal SRAM (aligned to 32-bit words)
-        pngBuffer = heap_caps_malloc(sizeof(PNG), MALLOC_CAP_INTERNAL | MALLOC_CAP_32BIT);
+        // Internal SRAM for the zero-wait-state access this decoder wants.
+        //
+        // Deliberately NOT MALLOC_CAP_32BIT: that does not mean "aligned to
+        // 32-bit words", it means "only 32-bit accesses are legal here", and on
+        // ESP32-S3 it can hand back IRAM. Constructing PNG() in place does
+        // byte-sized stores, which fault on such a region - StoreProhibited
+        // inside initPNGDecoder the moment the map screen is opened.
+        pngBuffer = heap_caps_malloc(sizeof(PNG), MALLOC_CAP_INTERNAL | MALLOC_CAP_8BIT);
 
         if (!pngBuffer) {
             ILOG_ERROR("Failed to allocate PNG context in Internal SRAM!");
